# React

Export named function components. Handlers inside a component are arrow functions.

Use `Show` for optional UI and `ListRenderer` for lists. Pass `keyOverride`.

Route strings live in `PATHS` under `apps/web-app/src/constants/paths.ts`.

App components live under `apps/web-app/src/components` in atomic folders. `@repo/ui` uses the same folders under `packages/ui/src/components`. Keep an empty folder with a `.gitkeep`.

- `atoms` — a single primitive, such as `button`, `Show`, and `ListRenderer`. The app folder stays empty while those primitives live in `@repo/ui`.
- `molecules` — a presentational group of primitives, such as `field` and `CreateNoteFields`
- `organisms` — a section that owns state or events, such as `CreateNoteForm`. The UI package folder stays empty until a shared section needs it.
- `templates` — a page layout that renders server props, such as `NotesPageTemplate`. The UI package folder stays empty until a shared layout needs it.
- `pages` — a screen assembled from a template. The Next.js route stays in `app`, so both page folders stay empty.

Page templates render props from the server. `"use client"` starts at the leaf that needs state or events. `useNotes` and later view-model hooks live in `@repo/data` and cover that interaction.

shadcn components live in `@repo/ui`. Add them with the shadcn CLI from `apps/web-app`. The `ui` alias writes into `@repo/ui/components/atoms`. If a file lands in the app, move it. Move a component that composes other primitives, such as `field`, into `molecules`.
